<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soulbury Constitution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1947</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Soulbury Constitution was the constitution of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a> drafted on the recommendations of the Soulbury Commission and brought into force in 1947–1948. It created a parliamentary system on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-system">Westminster model</a> and governed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> of Ceylon after independence in 1948, until the republican constitution of 1972 made the country <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>.</p></div>
